{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Ban insurance auto-renewal at a higher price without fresh consent",
        "additional_details": "Agreeing to automatic renewal should not mean agreeing to an unknown future price. When the price rises, customers should decide whether to renew after seeing the new amount. Require a clear comparison with the previous total price, a simple way to accept or decline, and advance warning if cover will end without consent. Silence or an old auto-renewal instruction should not count as agreement to the higher price.",
        "background": "Change the law to require insurers and brokers to obtain fresh, explicit consent before renewing a policy at a higher total price for the same, substantially similar or reduced cover. Include mandatory fees and finance charges and compare costs over the same period and payment basis.",
